.TH REDQUERY 1 "November 2026" "RedQuery" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
redquery \- automated Boolean-based SQL injection testing and extraction tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B redquery
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B RedQuery
is a Python-based tool for automating Boolean-based SQL injection testing and data extraction.

It supports GET and POST requests, AND and OR Boolean conditions, string and integer injection contexts, configurable request timeouts, output saving, and extraction resumption.

RedQuery uses a modular architecture in which different modules handle argument parsing, execution orchestration, payload generation, request dispatching, response verification, extraction, and resume operations.

The tool is intended for authorized security testing and controlled laboratory environments.
.SH FEATURES
.IP \(bu 2
Boolean-based SQL injection testing and extraction.
.IP \(bu 2
GET and POST request support.
.IP \(bu 2
AND and OR Boolean conditions.
.IP \(bu 2
String and integer injection contexts.
.IP \(bu 2
Configurable request timeout.
.IP \(bu 2
Custom output filename.
.IP \(bu 2
Resume interrupted extraction.
.IP \(bu 2
Verbose execution mode.
.IP \(bu 2
Optional SSL certificate verification bypass.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-url " " URL
Specifies the target URL.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-fail_message " " MESSAGE
Specifies the response message used as the failure indicator during response verification.
.TP
.BR \-\-method " " METHOD
Specifies the HTTP request method.
.br
Supported methods: GET and POST.
.br
The default method is POST.
.TP
.BR \-\-data " " DATA
Specifies the POST request data.
.br
Example: "username=test&password=test".
.TP
.BR \-\-param " " PARAMETER
Specifies the parameter to be tested.
.TP
.BR \-\-condition " " CONDITION
Specifies the Boolean condition used during injection.
.br
Supported values: AND and OR.
.br
The default condition is OR.
.TP
.BR \-\-context " " CONTEXT
Specifies the injection context.
.br
Supported values: string and int.
.br
The default context is string.
.TP
.BR \-\-valid " " VALUE
Specifies the valid value used by the injection logic.
.TP
.BR \-\-timeout " " SECONDS
Specifies the maximum time, in seconds, to wait for an HTTP response.
.br
The default timeout is 4 seconds.
.br
Increase this value when testing environments respond slowly.
.TP
.BR \-o " [" FILENAME ]
Enables saving extraction results.
.br
If a filename is supplied, it is used as the output filename.
.br
If no filename is supplied, the default filename is Redquery.txt.
.TP
.BR \-\-resume
Enables resume execution using previously saved extraction progress.
.TP
.BR \-\-enum " " STAGE
Specifies the enumeration stage to continue from when resume mode is enabled.
.TP
.BR \-v
Enables verbose mode and displays additional execution information.
.TP
.BR \-k
Disables SSL certificate verification.
.SH EXECUTION
RedQuery begins by parsing the supplied command-line arguments and determining whether normal or resume execution should be performed.

During normal execution, the application performs the required counting operations before starting extraction.

The extraction engine generates payloads and passes them to the verification module. The verification module communicates with the request module, which dispatches the appropriate GET or POST request.

The returned response is evaluated to determine whether the current Boolean condition is satisfied. This process repeats until the requested value has been reconstructed.

After extraction, the user can select a result to continue with another enumeration stage.

.SH RESUME FUNCTIONALITY
RedQuery supports resuming an interrupted extraction process.

The application stores extraction state in a JSON file named:
.PP
.B redquery.restore
.PP
When resume mode is enabled, RedQuery loads the saved data, restores the relevant extraction state, and continues the process.

The
.B --resume
option enables this functionality, while
.B --enum
specifies the enumeration stage to continue from.

Supported resume stages should match the stages implemented by the installed version of RedQuery.

.SH OUTPUT
When output saving is enabled with
.BR \-o ,
RedQuery writes extraction results to the specified file.

If no filename is provided, the default output filename is:
.PP
.B Redquery.txt
.PP
The restore file
.B redquery.restore
is used separately to preserve extraction progress for resume operations.

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B POST request using AND condition and string context:
.nf
redquery --url http://kitty.thm -m "Invalid username or password" \\
-o KittyOutput --timeout 5 --data "username=sds&password=sd" \\
--param username --condition AND --valid kitty
.fi
.TP
.B POST request using AND condition and integer context:
.nf
redquery --url http://kitty.thm -m "Invalid username or password" \\
--context int -o --timeout 5 --data "username=sds&password=sd" \\
--param username --condition AND --valid kitty
.fi
.TP
.B POST request using default OR condition and integer context:
.nf
redquery --url http://kitty.thm -m "Invalid username or password" \\
--context int -o KittyOutput --timeout 5 \\
--data "username=sds&password=sd" --param username -v
.fi
.TP
.B POST request with resume enabled:
.nf
redquery -u http://kitty.thm --fail_message "Invalid username or password" \\
-o Myoutputhere --data "username=sds&password=sd" \\
--param username --condition AND --valid kitty \\
--resume --enum table -k
.fi
.TP
.B GET request using default OR condition and integer context:
.nf
redquery --url http://kitty.thm?id= -m "Invalid username or password" \\
--method GET --context int -o --timeout 10 -v -k
.fi
.TP
.B GET request with resume enabled:
.nf
redquery -u http://kitty.thm?product_id= -m "Invalid product id" \\
--method GET -o Redqueryhere --resume --enum column \\
--valid 2 --condition AND
.fi
.SH ARCHITECTURE
RedQuery follows a modular architecture.

The main execution process is coordinated by the main, sub-main, checker, counter, and engine modules. Payload generation, request dispatching, and response verification are handled by dedicated modules.

The resume module restores previously saved extraction state before continuing the normal extraction workflow.

The config module provides shared configuration and extraction state to the modules that require it.

For detailed architecture diagrams and module interactions, refer to the architecture directory in the project repository.
.SH EXIT STATUS
An exit status of 0 indicates successful execution.
.br
A non-zero exit status indicates an error or unsuccessful execution.
.PP
Actual exit statuses depend on the conditions handled by the installed version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I redquery.restore
JSON file containing saved extraction state used by resume functionality.
.TP
.I Redquery.txt
Default output filename when output saving is enabled without a custom filename.
